From 15bcbd7a893b197376ca4a3b0fe54163bc5fcb46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 16:33:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make stage gate + plan issue creation kernel-native (bd
 optional)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Release blocker: all 6 workflow stages threw when the `bd` binary was
absent, even though the kernel is the default issue backend — breaking
the "no Beads install required" contract.

Root fix — bd is now conditional on the resolved issue backend:
- lib/runtime-health.js: checkRuntimeHealth resolves the issue backend
  (env > .forge/config.yaml > default 'kernel'). A missing bd is a
  hard-stop diagnostic ONLY when backend=beads; on kernel it is a
  non-blocking advisory (new `advisories` array). gh and jq stay
  unconditional hard requirements. Adds `checks.issueBackend`.
- lib/workflow/enforce-stage.js: resolves the backend and threads it
  into checkRuntimeHealth; adds an injectable `checkHealth` seam
  (consistent with the existing `health`/`repairRuntime` seams).

Kernel-native plan issue creation:
- lib/commands/plan.js: `forge plan` now routes issue creation through
  the kernel broker (runIssueOperation) when backend=kernel, instead of
  shelling to `bd create`. New `createKernelIssue`; executePlan resolves
  the backend and dispatches; the beads path (createBeadsIssue) is
  preserved for backend=beads. Extracts a shared description builder.

Tests (TDD): runtime-health (bd advisory on kernel, blocks on beads,
gh stays hard), enforce-stage (backend resolution + gate), plan
(createKernelIssue + executePlan kernel routing, no bd). Updated the
existing "missing bd" test to assert the beads path.

Regenerated docs/work/.../bd-call-site-kill-list.md (release-check D20
audit artifact) to reflect the new bd reference map.

Note: touched files renormalize CRLF->LF per .gitattributes (eol=lf);
pre-existing CRLF blobs cause EOL-only diff lines in test/commands/plan.test.js.

